# =============================================================================
# production-6 / ponder-indexer — PHASE 1 (Ankr), four chains only
# =============================================================================
# This file lives in the DApp repo for ops reference only. The real change set
# belongs in the Ponder indexer repo (e.g. github.com/socraticblock/ponder):
#   ponder.config.ts + Railway env — NOT done until implemented on a branch
#   there (see “Git / branch protection” below).
#
# =============================================================================
# CRITICAL — do not accidentally redeploy the working public Ponder API
# =============================================================================
# The working public Railway service (example name: `ponder`) must keep:
#   npx ponder serve --schema production-5
#
# If that service auto-deploys from `main` and someone merges a new
# `ponder.config.ts` (e.g. 4-chain indexer-only config), the deploy can break
# compatibility with the restored `production-5` snapshot API again.
#
# Safe rule:
#   main              = keep compatible with public `ponder serve` + production-5
#   feature branch    = all production-6 / 4-chain indexer experiments
#
# Do NOT merge the indexer branch to `main` until the experiment is validated
# and you have an explicit plan for `main` (if ever).
#
# =============================================================================
# Git / branch protection (Ponder repo: socraticblock/ponder)
# =============================================================================
# Before changing ponder.config.ts, protect the working API.
#
# Create a separate branch only for production-6 indexing, for example:
#   production-6-indexer-4chains
#
# On that branch ONLY:
#   1. Configure Ponder for phase 1 chains only: Ethereum, Base, Polygon, Arbitrum
#   2. Per-chain RPC URL env vars (not a single shared Alchemy-style key). Suggested:
#          RPC_URL_ETHEREUM
#          RPC_URL_BASE
#          RPC_URL_POLYGON
#          RPC_URL_ARBITRUM
#      (values can be Ankr URLs, e.g. https://rpc.ankr.com/eth/YOUR_ANKR_PROJECT_KEY)
#   3. Conservative ethGetLogsBlockRange (wire in ponder.config):
#          Ethereum  100
#          Base      25
#          Polygon   200
#          Arbitrum  750
#   4. MAX_REQUESTS_PER_SECOND=1
#   5. Run: yarn typecheck
#   6. Do NOT merge this branch to main yet.
#
# =============================================================================
# Railway
# =============================================================================
# - Public `ponder` service: unchanged; stays on main + production-5 serve.
# - Separate service `ponder-indexer`: connect ONLY to branch
#   production-6-indexer-4chains (or whatever you named it).
#   Start command:  npx ponder start --schema production-6
#
# Do not touch:
#   - public `ponder` service
#   - production-5
#   - Postgres / restored production-5 snapshot
#   - frontend / NEXT_PUBLIC_PONDER_URL
#
# If production-6 starts from scratch, that is expected. Watch catch-up for
# 429s and eth_getLogs range errors. On heavy failure, stop only ponder-indexer.
#
# =============================================================================
# Railway env (ponder-indexer) — placeholders only; never commit real keys
# =============================================================================
MAX_REQUESTS_PER_SECOND=1

RPC_URL_ETHEREUM=https://rpc.ankr.com/eth/YOUR_ANKR_PROJECT_KEY
RPC_URL_BASE=https://rpc.ankr.com/base/YOUR_ANKR_PROJECT_KEY
RPC_URL_POLYGON=https://rpc.ankr.com/polygon/YOUR_ANKR_PROJECT_KEY
RPC_URL_ARBITRUM=https://rpc.ankr.com/arbitrum/YOUR_ANKR_PROJECT_KEY

# Later (after the four chains are stable): Gnosis, Avalanche.
# Last (Ankr 403 in smoke tests until fixed): OP Mainnet, Sonic.

# If your ponder.config reads different names, alias in Railway or rename here.

# Postgres: DATABASE_URL can match production-5; --schema production-6 isolates tables.

# Watch: 429s, eth_getLogs range / max-result errors, schema/build mismatch, backfill explosions.
